---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import siteConfig, { formatPageTitle } from "../data/siteConfig";

const title = formatPageTitle("Privacy Policy");
const description = `How ${siteConfig.bandNameFormal} collects, uses, and protects information submitted through this website.`;
const email = siteConfig.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  effectiveDate="September 10, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This website is operated by The Electric Lavender Train (“we,” “us,” or “our”). This policy
    explains what information is handled when you use this website, its inquiry forms, newsletter
    signup, embedded media, or event-media submission link.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={siteConfig.routes.contactBooking}>Contact & Booking</a> page offers Booking,
    Merchandise, General, and Content Removal Request forms. Depending on the form, we may ask for
    your name, email address, optional phone number, organization or venue, event type and date,
    city or venue location, audience size, budget, song requests, merchandise details, a subject,
    a message, or information identifying content you want us to review. The removal form accepts
    an optional web address but no file upload.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not submit payment card numbers, government identification numbers, medical information, or
    other sensitive information through these forms. Submitting a booking inquiry does not confirm
    availability or create a booking. Submitting a removal request starts a review and does not
    guarantee removal.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you email us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, Google handles the message
    through Gmail and we receive whatever information you choose to include.
  </p>

  <h2>How inquiry forms work</h2>
  <p>
    A working inquiry form sends your submission directly from your browser to Formspree. Formspree
    processes the form, may retain a copy, applies its spam and CAPTCHA controls, and sends an email
    notification to us. Formspree may also receive technical information normally associated with
    a web request, such as your IP address, browser or device information, submission time, and
    referring page. An inquiry never subscribes you to the newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to booking, merchandise, general, and content-removal inquiries;</li>
    <li>To communicate about a potential or confirmed engagement;</li>
    <li>To operate the newsletter when you separately request it;</li>
    <li>To review event media you voluntarily submit;</li>
    <li>To prevent spam, abuse, and security incidents; and</li>
    <li>To keep records reasonably needed for business, accounting, dispute, or legal purposes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, use inquiry information for behavioral advertising, or
    add inquiry senders to a marketing list without separate consent.
  </p>

  <h2>Newsletter signup</h2>
  <p>
    When the newsletter link is available, it opens a form hosted by Brevo rather than a form on
    this website. The form collects your email address for one weekly ELT schedule newsletter.
    It does not offer a separate show-alert list or preference. Signup uses double opt-in: Brevo
    sends a confirmation message, and you are not subscribed until you confirm.
  </p>
  <p>
    The hosted form may use Google reCAPTCHA to distinguish people from automated submissions.
    When it does, Google may receive technical information about your visit and interaction under
    Google's own terms and privacy policy. Brevo may process delivery, bounce, open, and link-click
    information according to the settings applied to our account and Brevo's own practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every newsletter includes an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing stops marketing delivery and
    places the address on the applicable suppression list so it is not accidentally mailed or
    re-imported without a valid new consent. You may also contact us to request deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Event-media submissions</h2>
  <p>
    When the “Share Your Event Media” link is available, it opens a Google Form. The upload and
    consent process occurs on Google's systems, not this website. Google may require sign-in and
    may associate the response with your Google account. The form may collect your contact
    information, event details, uploaded photos or video, and your response to the consent and
    permission terms displayed on that form.
  </p>
  <p>
    Submission does not guarantee publication. Do not submit media you lack permission to share.
    Do not submit media whose primary subject is a child. Media containing other identifiable
    people may require additional permission and may be declined.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers and external services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Formspree</strong> processes configured inquiry forms and delivers notifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> provides Gmail, Google Forms/Drive where enabled, reCAPTCHA where displayed, and YouTube.</li>
    <li><strong>Brevo</strong> hosts the newsletter form and manages subscriptions and email delivery when enabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Sanity</strong> stores public editorial content; it does not receive inquiry or newsletter submissions.</li>
    <li><strong>Our website host</strong> serves the site and may keep routine access and security logs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Links to social, ticketing, streaming, pre-save, payment/tipping, and other third-party sites
    take you to services with their own terms and privacy practices. We do not control those
    services.
  </p>

  <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
  <p>
    Embedded videos use YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain and do not create a player until you
    choose to activate one. After activation, YouTube/Google processes the interaction under its
    own policies and may display advertising. Privacy-enhanced mode reduces requests before
    activation but does not eliminate third-party processing after you play a video.
  </p>

  <h2>Website logs, cookies, and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Our host may process standard access and security information such as IP address, requested
    page, timestamp, and browser details. We do not configure first-party analytics, advertising
    pixels, remarketing tools, or behavioral-advertising cookies on this website. External hosted
    pages and an activated YouTube player may use their own cookies or similar technologies.
    If we add non-essential tracking to this website, we will update this policy and review whether
    consent controls are required before enabling it.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Inquiries:</strong> retained only as reasonably necessary to respond, manage a
      potential or confirmed engagement, maintain appropriate records, resolve disputes, handle
      removal requests, and meet legal obligations. Closed inquiries are periodically reviewed and
      deleted when there is no reasonable need to keep them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Newsletter:</strong> active subscription information is retained while you remain
      subscribed. After unsubscribe, a limited suppression record may be retained to honor the
      opt-out and prevent accidental resubscription.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Event media:</strong> unselected original uploads are targeted for deletion within
      approximately one month. Selected media and the associated permission record may be retained
      as reasonably necessary to support authorized use.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Provider records:</strong> security logs and backups controlled by a provider may
      follow that provider's retention schedule and may not disappear immediately.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Retention reviews are performed by people; this website does not run an automatic deletion
    system. Any export we create is subject to the same retention decision as its source.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask to access, correct, or delete information you submitted by emailing
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. For published content, you may also use the
    Content Removal Request form. We will review the request and may retain information when
    reasonably required for a contract, accounting, dispute, security, or legal obligation.
    Newsletter recipients can unsubscribe through the link in any newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable administrative and provider-supported safeguards, but no internet
    transmission or storage system is completely secure. Please use the contact methods above if
    you believe information has been submitted or exposed improperly.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This website and its forms are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
    collect personal information from children under 13. Contact us if you believe a child has
    submitted information or appears in submitted media so we can review it.
  </p>

  <h2>California and international visitors</h2>
  <p>
    The categories of personal information handled are limited to the identifiers, inquiry
    content, subscription information, submitted media, and technical information described above.
    We do not sell this information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. The site
    is operated from the United States; information may be processed in the United States or other
    locations where our providers operate.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as our website or services change. A material revision will be shown
    by changing the effective date above.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or privacy requests may be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
